      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, the relative amplitude or volume of each overtone is crucial; the specific spectral fingerprint is what we perceive as a unique timbre. \"Ghost notes\" or unintended sounds are often related to complex interactions within the instrument's acoustics, sometimes involving subtle, inharmonic partials not strictly belonging to the ideal harmonic series. These unwanted vibrations can occur due to imperfect bore designs or how the player initiates the sound.",
